    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's just frustrating because when you say \"no scientific evidence\" it feels like you're dismissing something i am literally living through. if it's just \"psychological\" then why does it feel like my actual DNA is responding to the environment? i feel like there's this latent capacity inside me that's trying to wake up and the more i try to ignore it, the louder the vibrations get. i really need to figure out how to manage this transition. if i were to try and decrease the external \"noise\" to see if i can focus this new perception, how would one even begin to structure a sensory deprivation protocol for something like this?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
